PATCH 335: FUN_0000_b5e7 (+ its mid-entry twin b60f) -- the object-type-F per-frame UPDATE method
dispatched by the c0e5 -0x1bac object-update loop (patch 243).  FULL object-relative reconstruction: the
object (DI) was bound to the never-threaded param_5 -> SIGSEGV on the ACCEPT flight tick.  The b355/b51f
family, and the FIRST crash on the ACCEPT flight tick under ASLR-off.

THE CRASH (deterministic, `setarch -R` + warm datadir, default `make native` AZER1 ACCEPT
BATTLES(160,100)->OK(205,128)->ACCEPT(40,186), FIST_COOP_TICK=1 FIST_TICK_HZ=25000):
  459a -> c0ca -> c0e5 -> b5e7,  fault-addr 0x2d then (deeper) the `mov bx,[di]` unaff_CS deref, 5/5 runs.

ROOT CAUSE (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin @ 0xb5e7-0xb6c8; DS=SS=DGROUP=0x1c00; CS=0):
b5e7 is a per-type object UPDATE method reached from c0e5 (`mov di,[si]; mov bx,[di]; shl bx,1;
call [bx-0x1bac]`, DI=object near offset live, SI=list cursor live -- patch 243).  Ghidra bound b5e7's
DI varnode to param_5 (c0e5 threads only DI, as param_1 -> param_5 uninitialised/null under ASLR-off ->
top `*(int*)(param_5+0x2d)` faults) and the SI varnode to param_4; it ALSO lost e1a6's sign flag (the
`js b691` explosion-init branch), lost bb1b's CF (`jb b653`), and emitted a spurious
`unaff_CS = &DAT_1000_cf69` in place of the `mov bx,[di]` object-word0 reads (so `*unaff_CS*2-0x6423`
faults once past the top).  Same class as the sibling c0e5 methods 7c1d/87df/b355/97d5/b51f
(patches 244/250/251/252/253).

THE FIX (full reconstruction, all asm-cited inline):
  - object = g_mem+0x1c000+di (di = param_1); every [di+off] read/store at its asm width (WORD/DWORD/BYTE).
  - the b691 branch's `mov bx,[di]; mov ax,[bx-0x6423]` rebased to word[DGROUP:(word0*2-0x6423)] (was
    the spurious unaff_CS host deref); param_5=unaff_CS artifacts dropped (the object never changes).
  - e1a6 returns a signed char -> `(char)e1a6(...) < 0` reproduces `js b691` (Ghidra folded it to the
    always-false bVar3, so it took the b691 branch whenever [di+0xd]<0x80 regardless of e1a6).
  - bb1b returns CF via g_fist_cf -> `jb b653` faithful (Ghidra's bVar3=false always returned).
  - the destruct-branch DAT_2000_5bd7 = (-[di+0x10]-[si+0x10])>>0xc uses the LIVE c0e5 cursor SI,
    published by c0e5 in the shim global g_fist_c0e5_si (the __allregs dispatch threads only DI).
  - the tail b354/b2ef (lcall 0xf69:0xbcc4/0xbc5f) takes the object.

Mission-cascade only (the in-mission 459a flight tick) -> behaviour-neutral for the 24 menu/settings
verify flows.  b60f (a Ghidra mid-function entry that shares b5e7's tail body) carries the same class;
it is a separate decompiled fn and is threaded next if it surfaces.

